{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AzHtEaYoGp1zyF9tNizagt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Mathlib\n2\t\n3\topen BigOperators Finset Matrix\n4\t\n5\t/--\n6\tFor $n \\geq 2$, let $A = [a_{i,j}]_{i,j=1}^n$ be an $n$-by-$n$ matrix of nonnegative integers such that:\n7\t(a) $a_{i,j} = 0$ when $i + j \\leq n$;\n8\t(b) $a_{i+1,j} \\in \\{a_{i,j}, a_{i,j} + 1\\}$ when $1 \\leq i \\leq n-1$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n$; and\n9\t(c) $a_{i,j+1} \\in \\{a_{i,j}, a_{i,j} + 1\\}$ when $1 \\leq i \\leq n$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n-1$.\n10\t\n11\tLet $S$ be the sum of the entries of $A$, and let $N$ be the number of nonzero entries of $A$.\n12\tProve that $S \\leq \\frac{(n+2)N}{3}$.\n13\t-/\n14\ttheorem putnam_2025_b4\n15\t    (m : ℕ)\n16\t    (A : Matrix (Fin (m + 2)) (Fin (m + 2)) ℕ)\n17\t    (ha : ∀ (i j : Fin (m + 2)), (i : ℕ) + (j : ℕ) ≤ m → A i j = 0)\n18\t    (hb : ∀ (i : Fin (m + 1)) (j : Fin (m + 2)),\n19\t      A (Fin.succ i) j = A (Fin.castSucc i) j ∨\n20\t      A (Fin.succ i) j = A (Fin.castSucc i) j + 1)\n21\t    (hc : ∀ (i : Fin (m + 2)) (j : Fin (m + 1)),\n22\t      A i (Fin.succ j) = A i (Fin.castSucc j) ∨\n23\t      A i (Fin.succ j) = A i (Fin.castSucc j) + 1)\n24\t    (S : ℕ)\n25\t    (hS : S = ∑ i : Fin (m + 2), ∑ j : Fin (m + 2), A i j)\n26\t    (N : ℕ)\n27\t    (hN : N = #{p : Fin (m + 2) × Fin (m + 2) | A p.1 p.2 ≠ 0}) :\n28\t    3 * S ≤ (m + 4) * N := by\n29\t  sorry\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6801b411-0b45-4811-a180-f34ddfaf361f","uuid":"4b41f381-cb0f-4f2e-9d9f-8f0384c25aa9","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:12:23.257Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/putnam_2025_b4.lean","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen BigOperators Finset Matrix\n\n/--\nFor $n \\geq 2$, let $A = [a_{i,j}]_{i,j=1}^n$ be an $n$-by-$n$ matrix of nonnegative integers such that:\n(a) $a_{i,j} = 0$ when $i + j \\leq n$;\n(b) $a_{i+1,j} \\in \\{a_{i,j}, a_{i,j} + 1\\}$ when $1 \\leq i \\leq n-1$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n$; and\n(c) $a_{i,j+1} \\in \\{a_{i,j}, a_{i,j} + 1\\}$ when $1 \\leq i \\leq n$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n-1$.\n\nLet $S$ be the sum of the entries of $A$, and let $N$ be the number of nonzero entries of $A$.\nProve that $S \\leq \\frac{(n+2)N}{3}$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2025_b4\n    (m : ℕ)\n    (A : Matrix (Fin (m + 2)) (Fin (m + 2)) ℕ)\n    (ha : ∀ (i j : Fin (m + 2)), (i : ℕ) + (j : ℕ) ≤ m → A i j = 0)\n    (hb : ∀ (i : Fin (m + 1)) (j : Fin (m + 2)),\n      A (Fin.succ i) j = A (Fin.castSucc i) j ∨\n      A (Fin.succ i) j = A (Fin.castSucc i) j + 1)\n    (hc : ∀ (i : Fin (m + 2)) (j : Fin (m + 1)),\n      A i (Fin.succ j) = A i (Fin.castSucc j) ∨\n      A i (Fin.succ j) = A i (Fin.castSucc j) + 1)\n    (S : ℕ)\n    (hS : S = ∑ i : Fin (m + 2), ∑ j : Fin (m + 2), A i j)\n    (N : ℕ)\n    (hN : N = #{p : Fin (m + 2) × Fin (m + 2) | A p.1 p.2 ≠ 0}) :\n    3 * S ≤ (m + 4) * N := by\n  sorry\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AzHtEaYoGp1zyF9tNizagt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
